10. [Maximum mark: 11]
Consider the function $f$, defined by $f(x) = x - a\sqrt{x}$, where $x \ge 0$, $a \in \mathbb{R}^+$.
(a) Find in terms of $a$
(i) the zeros of $f$;
(ii) the values of $x$ for which $f$ is decreasing;
(iii) the values of $x$ for which $f$ is increasing;
(iv) the range of $f$. [10 marks]
(b) State the concavity of the graph of $f$. [1 mark]
